{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 8, :comments ["<b>Do, men.</b> The plural masculine and feminine forms in the past-tense verb without additions are equal, with an open vav [i.e., cholam]." "<b>Ha-El.</b> Like ha-Elohim. The Gaon [Saadia] says that because the third [person] did not appear, he said thus. This reason is far-fetched, for both expressions are also found in the Aramaic language."], :book :genesis, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 19, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"] ["Piotrkow, 1907-1911" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH990020973480205171/NLI"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:45:05.826512904Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}